./LOGBOOK.md:195:- FINDING: a green `Implementations` lane is not by itself proof the gate ran — `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` is a job-level env in `implementations.yml`, and `golden_test.go:29` **skips** the whole suite when it is unset. Checked at test granularity instead: run `30616107892` logs `--- PASS: TestManagerLifecycleVectors` and `--- PASS: TestManagerCompiledCacheMissDryRunVector` on ubuntu, macOS *and* windows. Worth repeating for any future conformance-gate acceptance.
./LOGBOOK.md:339:- NOTE: reviewer full suite was 950 passed/86 skipped vs the implementer's 1116/38 — the gap is entirely `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` not being exported, so the pinned conformance suite skips. Check that env var before treating a pytest count delta as a regression.
./LOGBOOK.md:651:- FINDING (F3): a Make target labelled "mirrors the CI gate exactly" ran `go test ./...` with `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` **unset**, so every conformance test silently skipped, and it added a Linux-only guard the macOS/Windows job never runs. A `require-pin-root` guard now makes the root a hard input for every suite target. **A green gate that skipped the tests it claims to run is worse than a red one.**
./LOGBOOK.md:706:- FINDING: the composite is statically red on **all three** platforms under the committed pin, and Linux is only the third-largest cause. Six conformance sites read an rc.5-only artifact and `t.Fatal` when it is missing — they skip only when `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` is *unset*, not when the artifact is absent: `buildsource/conformance_test.go:16`, `buildcache/conformance_test.go:15`+`readJSONObject:63`, `scopes/gc_conformance_test.go:38`, `marker/marker_v2_test.go:37`, `whitelist/conformance_test.go:20,25`, `skillspec/conformance_test.go:106`. CI exports the root for `go test ./...`. Verified by `git cat-file -e` per path per revision, not inferred.
./LOGBOOK.md:738:- DECISION: `TASK-260729-35tb37` rework cycle 1 added a required regression gate to the schema-v6 root plan — `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT=<rc.3>/conformance/v1 pytest tests/test_protocol_conformance.py::test_skill_manifest_resolution_vectors` — instead of relying on `tests/test_skillspec.py`. Reason: schema 6 rewrites `_load_skill_manifest()`, the exact seam whose earlier gap produced a *silent empty spec*, and producer-authored cases written in the same commit can regress in lockstep with the parser. The eight rc.3 vectors are owner-published, so they cannot.
./LOGBOOK.md:741:- TRAP: `tests/test_protocol_conformance.py` carries `pytestmark = pytest.mark.skipif(not ROOT_TEXT, …)`. A bare local run of that module skips everything and exits 0. Any gate citing it must export `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` or it proves nothing.
./LOGBOOK.md:767:- FINDING: the rc.5 candidate cannot be pinned as a revision. `.temp/TASK-260729-3nx97g/worktree` is an *uncommitted* curator-spec tree (3 modified, 18 untracked) on top of `v1.0.0-rc.3`. Only `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` + manifest digest `b6f56aac…04c` (verified) identify it. A hosted GitHub runner cannot reach that path, so candidate jobs are either self-hosted or locally-executed evidence — writing a hosted candidate job that can never fire would be a false gate.
./LOGBOOK.md:808:- FINDING (structural): `schemas/v1/` lives **outside** `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` and is not covered by `conformance/v1/manifest.json` (which covers only `schema-cases`, `expected`, `fixtures`, `vectors`). Every schema-derived assertion in the `12r55p` AC is instead satisfiable from manifest-covered `schema-cases/`, so no `jsonschema` dependency and no second oracle is introduced.
./LOGBOOK.md:809:- DECISION: cluster gating is **fail-on-missing, never skip-on-missing**. Parity-map §3.3 documented Curator's `TestCandidateBuildMetadataArtifacts` silently SKIPping for the whole rc.5 candidate line while reporting exit 0. The Python harness declares a per-cluster introducing protocol version: below it → honest skip naming both versions; at or above it with the files absent → hard `AssertionError`.
